.TH "TIMEEVENT.DETAIL" "3JS" "April 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
TimeEvent.detail \- TimeEvent: detail property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]TimeEvent.detail\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property provides
contextual information about the event, depending on the event type.
.PP
For \f[CR]repeatEvent\f[R] events, \f[CR]detail\f[R] contains the
current repeat iteration as a non\-negative integer.
Because the event is not raised for the first iteration, the value will
always be 1 or greater.
.PP
For \f[CR]beginEvent\f[R] and \f[CR]endEvent\f[R] events,
\f[CR]detail\f[R] is always \f[CR]0\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]long\f[R].
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]TimeEvent\f[R]
